# Kaggle experiment workspace (kx)

Driven by the `kaggle-exp` skill through the `kx` CLI. Every `kx` command prints one
JSON object whose `next_action` says what to do next; `kx status` recomputes it.

- `control/` — config, state (incl. the validation status), competition profile
  (`profile.json`), the data facts from `kx diagnose` (`facts.json`) and the derived
  `ledger.jsonl` (one line per experiment, rebuilt from `experiments/*/meta.json`).
- `experiments/exp-NNN/` — `experiment.json` (the declaration), the code file
  (`train.py`; `predict.py` for an inference stage, `main.py` for a simulation agent),
  `meta.json` (the recorded result), `VERDICT.md` (the written verdict) and `output/`
  (pulled kernel outputs; heavy files are gitignored).
- `control/submissions.jsonl` — every proposed and confirmed submission with its
  leaderboard read-back.
- `research/` — notes on discussions, notebooks and the host metric (raw cache
  uncommitted); `writeup/` — the checklist for writeup competitions.
- `strategy.md` — regenerated each cycle: current best, tried-list digest, reasoning.

Credentials never live here. A pre-commit hook (`.githooks/pre-commit`) blocks any
commit that contains a Kaggle credential.
